            <div xml:id="d788">

                <pb facs="0742" n="644" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg644"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Hardy.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June 6,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23. Greek Series.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 39, of the 19th ultimo, has been
                    received.</p>
                <p>The Department is unwilling to conclude with Greece a convention regulating the
                    naturalization of the citizens and subjects of the two countries, unless such
                    convention recognize the right of the individual to change his allegiance.</p>
                <p>In the case of Mr. Economopoulos, a naturalized American citizen held for
                    military service in Greece, the Department will await further developments.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
